---
title: Active play and asynchronous reflection substrate
---
flowchart TB
  accTitle: One active player acts while a background learner proposes evidence-linked procedures
  accDescr: One active player uses skills or ordinary input through the existing writer to windowed CDDA. Original receipts feed a bounded job mailbox. An advisory agent claims jobs and returns source linked proposals outside all input locks. Only the active player adopts procedure revisions through the existing memory writer. User Pause remains independent. The source and synthetic transport are implemented; actual concurrent graphical use remains a separate acceptance gate.
  P["Active player<br/>plan, act, observe, correct"] --> I["Skills or direct interaction"]
  I --> W["One existing input writer"]
  W --> G["Windowed CDDA"]
  G --> E["Canonical visible evidence<br/>receipts and unfinished Work"]
  E --> P
  E -. "Original cutoff and omissions" .-> Q["Bounded cached jobs<br/>claim and result collection"]
  Q -. "No input lock or model wait" .-> R["Advisory agent<br/>compare and propose procedures"]
  R -. "Versioned advice, warnings<br/>questions and retractions" .-> P
  P -. "Automatic use and outcome links<br/>optional interpretation" .-> E
  P --> M["Serialized accepted<br/>advisory-memory revision"]
  M --> E
  U["User Pause"] --> W
  classDef learner fill:#eef2ff,stroke:#4f46e5,color:#111827
  class R learner
